---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RandomnessLab from "../../components/RandomnessLab.tsx";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Diversification: Randomness"
  description="The noisy sequel to the waveforms tool: with real randomness, variance never fully cancels — and assets sometimes fall together."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool · Part 2</p>
    <h1>Diversification meets randomness</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      In <a href="/tools/waveforms">Part 1</a>, tidy waves cancelled almost
      perfectly. Real markets aren't tidy. Here each asset is a <em>noisy</em>,
      mean-reverting return series. The portfolio below still wobbles less than
      its parts — but the cancellation is never perfect, it changes every run,
      and every so often everything drops at once.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <RandomnessLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What's different from the waves</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>It's random.</strong> The theory bar (what diversification
          "should" deliver) and the actual bar (what this particular run gave
          you) rarely match — and the gap jumps around every time you hit
          <strong>New draw</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Nothing cancels perfectly.</strong> Even at strong negative
          correlation, the portfolio keeps a residual wobble. There is no truly
          risk-free blend of risky assets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Assets sink together.</strong> Watch the "fell together"
          figure. The higher the correlation, the more often every holding is
          down at the same moment — exactly when diversification helps least.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is still a simplified model — the randomness is well-behaved, with
        no fat tails or real history. To bring it all together with the efficient
        frontier, capital market line, and a distribution of outcomes, head to the
        <a href="/tools/portfolio">Portfolio Diversification Lab</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
